> the limit of sin x / x as x approaches 0
  note: what does "sin" apply to: read as sin(x) / ..., not sin(x / ...) (say "sin the quantity ..." for the second)
  ucas: it(x) = sin(x)/x
  ucas: limit it x -> 0
limit of it as x -> 0:
  0/0: L'Hôpital: lim (cos(x))/(1) = lim cos(x)
  = 1 (from both sides)
  numeric from the left (a - h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0.9983341665, 0.9999934896, 0.9999999746, 0.9999999999, 1, 1
    extrapolated (Richardson): 1 (estimated error 0): agrees
  numeric from the right (a + h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0.9983341665, 0.9999934896, 0.9999999746, 0.9999999999, 1, 1
    extrapolated (Richardson): 1 (estimated error 0): agrees
> the limit of (1 + 1/x)^x as x goes to infinity
  ucas: it(x) = (1 + 1/x)^x
  ucas: limit it x -> inf
limit of it as x -> inf:
  (1/x + 1)^x = exp((x)*log(1/x + 1))
  0*inf: x*log(1/x + 1) = (log(1/x + 1))/(1/x)
  0/0: L'Hôpital: lim (-1/(x^2*(1/x + 1)))/(-1/x^2) = lim x^2/(x^2*(1/x + 1))
  at inf: x^2 ~ 1|x|^2, x^2*(1/x + 1) ~ 1|x|^2
  = 2.718281828
  numeric (x = 10*2^k, k = 0..21): 2.59374246, 2.709835576, 2.717751104, 2.718248647, 2.718279755, 2.718281764
    extrapolated (Richardson): 2.71828182846 (estimated error 3e-16): agrees
> what does 1/x tend to as x goes to infinity
  ucas: it(x) = 1/x
  ucas: limit it x -> inf
limit of it as x -> inf:
