> limit of (x^2 - 1)/(x - 1) as x -> 1
  ucas: it(x) = (x^2 - 1)/(x - 1)
  ucas: limit it x -> 1
limit of it as x -> 1:
  0/0: L'Hôpital: lim (2x)/(1) = lim 2x
  = 2 (from both sides)
  numeric from the left (a - h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 1.9, 1.99375, 1.999609375, 1.999975586, 1.999998474, 1.999999952
    extrapolated (Richardson): 2 (estimated error 0): agrees
  numeric from the right (a + h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 2.1, 2.00625, 2.000390625, 2.000024414, 2.000001526, 2.000000048
    extrapolated (Richardson): 2 (estimated error 7e-17): agrees
> the limit of 1/x as x approaches 0 from the right
  ucas: it(x) = 1/x
  ucas: limit it x -> 0 from right
limit of it as x -> 0+ (from the right):
  1/x -> inf (the numerator -> 1, x -> 0+)
  = inf
  numeric from the right (a + h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 10, 160, 2560, 40960, 655360, 20971520
    the values grow without bound (+): agrees
> the limit of (sin x - x)/x^3 as x approaches 0
  note: what does "sin" apply to: read as sin(x) - ..., not sin(x - ...) (say "sin the quantity ..." for the second)
  ucas: it(x) = (sin(x) - x)/x^3
  ucas: limit it x -> 0
limit of it as x -> 0:
  0/0: L'Hôpital: lim (cos(x) - 1)/(3x^2) = lim (cos(x) - 1)/(3x^2)
  0/0: L'Hôpital: lim (-sin(x))/(6x) = lim -sin(x)/(6x)
  0/0: L'Hôpital: lim (-cos(x))/(6) = lim -cos(x)/6
  = -1/6 (from both sides)
  numeric from the left (a - h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): -0.1665833532, -0.1666663411, -0.1666666654, -0.1666666667, -0.1666666649, -0.1666545868
    extrapolated (Richardson): -0.166666666701 (estimated error 0): agrees
  numeric from the right (a + h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): -0.1665833532, -0.1666663411, -0.1666666654, -0.1666666667, -0.1666666649, -0.1666545868
    extrapolated (Richardson): -0.166666666701 (estimated error 0): agrees
> find the limit of (1 - cos x)/x^2 as x approaches 0
  ucas: it(x) = (1 - cos(x))/x^2
  ucas: limit it x -> 0
limit of it as x -> 0:
  0/0: L'Hôpital: lim (sin(x))/(2x) = lim sin(x)/(2x)
  0/0: L'Hôpital: lim (cos(x))/(2) = lim cos(x)/2
  = 1/2 (from both sides)
  numeric from the left (a - h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0.4995834722, 0.4999983724, 0.4999999936, 0.5, 0.4999999888, 0.5000114441
    extrapolated (Richardson): 0.5 (estimated error 4e-14): agrees
  numeric from the right (a + h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): 0.4995834722, 0.4999983724, 0.4999999936, 0.5, 0.4999999888, 0.5000114441
    extrapolated (Richardson): 0.5 (estimated error 4e-14): agrees
> the limit of x*sin(1/x) as x approaches 0
  ucas: it(x) = x*sin(1/x)
  ucas: limit it x -> 0
limit of it as x -> 0:
  1/x -> inf (the numerator -> 1, x -> 0+)
  1/x -> inf: sin(1/x) keeps oscillating between -1 and 1
  squeeze: x -> 0 times a bounded factor
  = 0 (from both sides)
  numeric from the left (a - h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): -0.05440211109, 0.001371407865, 0.0001514012217, -2.073123128e-06, -1.492192327e-06, 2.088386152e-08
    extrapolated (Richardson): 8.80983672472e-07 (estimated error 1e-08)
    the values approach 0 (|f - L| = 2e-08 at the last point; not smooth enough to extrapolate): agrees
  numeric from the right (a + h, h = 0.1*2^-k, k = 0..21): -0.05440211109, 0.001371407865, 0.0001514012217, -2.073123128e-06, -1.492192327e-06, 2.088386152e-08
